    "body_markdown": "# System Security Architecture\n\n## Threat Modeling and Hardening Boundaries\n\nThis architectural scratchpad documents the core directives of our hardened infrastructure. All external inputs must be validated with paranoid bounds checking. Volatile secrets exist only ephemerally in mutable byte arrays and are actively destroyed. Secrets must never leak across recent apps, clipboard, or crash dumps.\n\nWe mandate zero unauthenticated IPC exposure across microservices. Every intent payload is treated as potentially adversarial. Microservices communicate strictly over mutual TLS with cryptographically pinned certificates. Database connections require clean-db rollback isolation per test suite.\n\nAdditionally, all dependency updates must undergo supply-chain auditing and pass license compatibility checks before integration.",
    "body_sha256": "abcdef0502030405060708090a0b0c0d0e0f101112131415161718191a1b1c1d",
